    "assumptions": [],
    "summary": "New admin-only engagement page plus first-touch signup-source capture. Read-only queries over existing tables for the funnel, and one additive migration on the users table for the source columns.",
    "updated_at": 1786667586,
    "answers": {},
    "non_goals": [
      "No third-party analytics service. Separate decision for Chris.",
      "No privacy policy or cookie notice in this feature. DEFERRED, NOT DISMISSED: spec D8 records it as an open obligation that must be resolved before this reaches production, because the feature adds a persistent 14-day tracking cookie to a site with no disclosure surface.",
      "No first-touch plumbing through the MCP OAuth flow. A Reddit visitor whose first completed sign-in is via MCP is attributed to \"mcp\" and loses the campaign; stated on the page.",
      "No recovery of already-deleted history. The milestone backfill produces floors, not totals.",
      "No cohort retention grid.",
      "No changes to /admin/reports."
    ],
    "acceptance_criteria": [
      "Admin-only page at /admin/engagement, in the Platform admin submenu, 403 for a non-admin.",
      "A milestone row is written exactly once per user per milestone; a second attempt is a silent no-op, not an error.",
      "A milestone survives deletion of the row that caused it: connection-setup GC, seat-hold release, agent hard-delete, and admin match delete.",
      "A human player (agent kind=human, no connection ever) is counted at set_up_a_way_to_play, joined_match, played_turn and returned. This is the DEFAULT new-user path and revisions 1-2 were blind to it.",
      "An MCP user who connects before building an agent is counted at both milestones in either order, with no invented drop.",
      "Milestone counts are independent: no count is suppressed because an earlier milestone is missing. There is no strict nesting.",
      "ai_connected is also reported as a share of users who chose an AI agent, not as a share of all signups.",
      "played_turn is NOT recorded for a defaulted submission, a NULL-submitted_at submission, or an autopilot submission.",
      "Bots and internal users are excluded from every number on the page via the stored users.is_internal flag.",
      "is_internal is set at all three in-app user-creation sites, and the migration backfill and the creation rule share ONE predicate so they cannot disagree.",
      "is_internal survives sync_google_user rewriting the email AND survives promote_user/demote_user changing the role.",
      "First touch survives later navigation and the Google OAuth round trip, and is cleared on sign-out so a second user in the same browser does not inherit it.",
      "MCP-created users record channel \"mcp\" in a dedicated first_source_channel column; a genuine ?utm_source=mcp does not collide with it.",
      "A user with no captured source renders as \"unknown\", never as \"direct\".",
      "Every people-count is COUNT(DISTINCT users.id).",
      "Return detection uses the page window timezone, and the window control defaults to the browser timezone rather than UTC.",
      "Smoke-test matches (TEST_NAME_PREFIX) are excluded, matching the existing /admin/reports filter.",
      "Stuck list labels users with no handle, caps at 50 rows, and shows a remainder count.",
      "The page renders two explanatory notes: milestones before the deploy date are reconstructed and undercount abandonment; and MCP-first signups lose their original campaign attribution.",
      "Migration is additive and reversible; alembic upgrade head then downgrade runs clean on SQLite.",
      "admin/users/{id} toggles is_internal BOTH ways, renders that control for floor-admin targets, and audit-logs via two new AdminAction values; admin/users shows an internal column.",
      "Milestone recording and first-touch capture are advisory: a failure logs and never breaks the request that triggered it."
    ],
    "checklist": {
      "goal": "Give platform admins one page showing where new users fall out of the signup-to-playing journey, and which traffic source each signup came from, so the next week of work targets the biggest measured leak instead of a hunch.",
      "audience": "Platform admins only, behind require_platform_admin. Not public and not shown to normal users. Chris is the only regular reader today, so at 10-20 users named rows matter more than percentages.",
      "constraints": "Async routes and async DB calls only. Dev DB is SQLite, prod is Postgres, so constraint operations in the migration must use op.batch_alter_table. Migrations additive and reversible. UPDATED rev3: first-touch capture DOES set a persistent session cookie on anonymous visitors (Chris decision, spec D8) - the earlier no-cookie constraint is withdrawn. The site has no privacy policy or cookie notice; spec D8 records this as an OPEN OBLIGATION that must be resolved before production, not before implementation. Follow app/read_models/admin_reports.py for query modules and app/services/admin_user_actions.py for admin action contracts.",
      "silent_risk": "yes",
      "silent_risk_note": "A wrong funnel still renders a clean page. Already hit this concretely: counting each step independently made the funnel go UP in the middle (11 users had connected an AI but 13 had joined a match) because users who archived an agent dropped out of one step but not the next. Source capture has the same shape - the UTM tag is gone from the URL by the time the user clicks sign in, and the Google OAuth round trip drops query params, so a naive implementation silently records NULL for every signup, passes tests, and looks fine in prod.",
      "design_settled": "no",
      "design_settled_note": "Page layout is settled from the design conversation (four summary numbers, nested funnel, stuck-people list, source table). The capture half is NOT settled: whether first touch is recorded in middleware or at the login route, how it survives the Google OAuth redirect, what string counts as a source, and how crawler traffic is excluded are all open questions.",
      "completeness_risk": "yes",
      "completeness_risk_note": "The signup-source value threads through first-touch capture, the session, sync_google_user, a users-table migration, the read model, and the template. Separately the bot-vs-agent and admin/test-account exclusion filter must be applied identically in every count on the page, or the four summary numbers will contradict the funnel below them."
    },
    "unresolved": []
  },
